<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Juan Pío de Tristán</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1773–1860</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Juan Pío de Tristán was a wealthy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arequipa">Arequipa</a> landowner and royalist general who served as the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> briefly in 1824, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ayacucho">Battle of Ayacucho</a>. He later accepted independence and became president of the South Peruvian Republic within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andres-de-santa-cruz">Andrés de Santa Cruz</a>'s Peru-Bolivian Confederation in 1838 and 1839.</p></div>
